  76:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Clock/Std/IfxClock.h ****  * The module initialisation can be done in the same function. Here an example:
  77:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Clock/Std/IfxClock.h ****  * \code
  78:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Clock/Std/IfxClock.h ****  *
  79:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Clock/Std/IfxClock.h ****  *        // standard PLL & clock initialisation
  80:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Clock/Std/IfxClock.h ****  *         IfxClock_init(&IfxClock_testClockConfig);
  81:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Clock/Std/IfxClock.h ****  * \endcode
  82:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Clock/Std/IfxClock.h ****  *
  83:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Clock/Std/IfxClock.h ****  *    The SYS PLL, PER PLL1, PLL2, PLL3 and clocks are now initialised based on the XTAL and PLL va
  84:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Clock/Std/IfxClock.h ****  *
  85:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Clock/Std/IfxClock.h ****  * Alternately the PLL and clocks can be initialised using below method which provides greater cont
